@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n03. Governance and Artifact Build | UC-10..14
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #FFF6DF
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "author : DecisionAuthor" as Author <<actor>>
object "reviewer : AuthorizedReviewer" as Reviewer <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "validator : DecisionValidator" as Validator
object "release : Release" as Release
object "policy : GovernancePolicy" as Policy
object "evidence : ApprovalAuditStore" as Evidence
object "builder : ArtifactBuilder" as Builder
object "artifacts : ArtifactStore" as Store
Author --> API : 1: submit(candidate revision)
API --> Auth : 1.1: authorize submit\n2.1: authorize review role and scope
API --> Validator : 1.2 [authorized]: validate candidate revision
API --> Release : 1.3 [valid]: submit(revision)\n2.2 [authorized]: review(command, actor, revision)
Release --> Policy : 1.3.1: calculateRisk(change, breaking, 30-day traffic)
Release --> Release : 1.3.2: bind revision; enter In Review\n2.2.1: check maker exclusion, stage and revision
Reviewer --> API : 2 *[while In Review]: approve/reject/increase tier
Release --> Policy : 2.2.2 [eligible command]: evaluate approval or upward override
Release --> Evidence : 2.2.3 [accepted]: append immutable review/override
Release --> Release : 2.2.4 [accepted]: update requirements / status
Release --> Builder : 2.2.5 [Approved and valid]: build(exact revision)
Builder --> Store : 2.2.5.1 [build succeeds]: store immutable artifact and manifest
API ..> Author : 1.4: submission status / error
API ..> Reviewer : 2.3: review status / error
note bottom of Policy
Tier 1: one Domain Approver.
Tier 2: Domain Peer THEN Workspace Owner.
Tier 3: Domain Owner AND Compliance Officer.
Maker cannot approve in any role; risk cannot decrease.
Only accepted commands produce review/override evidence.
end note
note bottom of Release
Reject returns candidate to Draft.
Approval requires all current stages/quorum.
Override re-evaluates required approvals;
approval reuse needs a policy decision.
Approved does not mean Active.
Build failure produces no deliverable artifact.
end note
legend bottom
  Nested sequence numbers show logical order; routine returns are omitted.
  * denotes repetition; [condition] guards a message; ..> is a reply.
  Each review is a separate request, not a long-running HTTP call.
endlegend
@enduml
